<%# Floating save bar for the Superuser tabs, mirroring blocks/home/stickySubmitBar.ejs
    (the one Monitor Settings uses). `.sticky-bar` is position:fixed, and because it sits
    inside the tab's own `.page-tab` it disappears with the tab like the rest of the content.
    An anchor rather than a submit button on purpose: every super tab binds
    `enclosure.find('.submit').click(...)` and calls form.submit() itself, so a native submit
    button here would fire the save twice. The spacer keeps the last field clear of the bar. %>
<div style="margin-bottom: 50px;"></div>
<div class="sticky-bar p-3">
    <a href="#" class="submit btn btn-sm btn-success" style="min-width: 150px"><i class="fa fa-check"></i> <%- lang.Save %></a>
</div>
